---
import DesignSystemShell from "../../layouts/DesignSystemShell.astro";
import DsSection from "../../components/design-system/DsSection.astro";
import DsRule from "../../components/design-system/DsRule.astro";
import DsSpec from "../../components/design-system/DsSpec.astro";
import DsToken from "../../components/design-system/DsToken.astro";
// The cash-family stylesheet is the shareable copy of the canonical board vocabulary
// (.fw on Friday WIP/AR is page-scoped). Importing it lets the board specimens below
// render with production CSS rather than a re-creation.
import "../../styles/cash-surface.css";

const jobs = [
  ["J-10412", "Anderson re-roof", "Denver", "R. Ortiz", "$18,420.00", "$4,200.00", "Sep 19", "Collect"],
  ["J-10398", "Maple St. hail", "Denver", "T. Nguyen", "$27,900.00", "$27,900.00", "Sep 26", "Invoice"],
  ["J-10377", "Willow Ct. gutters", "Denver", "R. Ortiz", "$3,150.00", "$0.00", "—", "Closed"],
  ["J-10360", "Birch Ave. siding", "Fort Collins", "A. Patel", "$41,000.00", "$12,500.00", "Oct 3", "Collect"],
  ["J-10351", "Elm Dr. re-roof", "Denver", "T. Nguyen", "$22,780.00", "$22,780.00", "Sep 30", "Invoice"],
];
---

<DesignSystemShell slug="components" source="app/command-center/src/styles/global.css">
  <p class="ds-callout is-info">
    <b>How to read a specimen</b>
    Every frame below is production markup styled by production CSS. Switch the theme in the top bar to see the dark
    variant. The code in each frame's header is the selector to use; anatomy and states follow, then the rule cards at
    the end carry the ids to cite.
  </p>

  <DsSection id="buttons" title="Buttons">
    <p>Four variants in a strict hierarchy. Exactly one primary per viewport (C-02). Buttons are sentence case, 800 weight, 44px minimum height in the shell, 30px for the small size on boards.</p>
    <DsSpec label="Shell buttons" code=".button + .button-primary | -secondary | -ghost | -danger">
      <button class="button button-primary">Approve credit memo</button>
      <button class="button button-secondary">Run audit</button>
      <button class="button button-ghost">Reset demo state</button>
      <button class="button button-danger">Reject</button>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Small size and disabled" code=".button-small · :disabled keeps pointer events for the tooltip">
      <button class="button button-primary button-small">Approve</button>
      <button class="button button-secondary button-small">Download pack</button>
      <button class="button button-ghost button-small">Filter</button>
      <button class="button button-secondary button-small" style="opacity:.45;filter:grayscale(.2);cursor:not-allowed" title="No data — greyed with tooltip, pointer events kept alive" aria-disabled="true">Process (no data)</button>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Board buttons" code=".cfx-btn · .cfx-btn-primary (board-local primary, teal)" layout="block">
      <div class="cfx" style="margin:0;padding:12px;min-height:0;border-radius:8px"><div class="cfx-toolbar"><a class="cfx-btn" href="#buttons">Download pack</a><a class="cfx-btn" href="#buttons">Accrual snapshot CSV</a><button class="cfx-btn cfx-btn-primary" type="button">Email via Maya</button></div></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Fill / ink</th><th>Use</th><th>Hover</th><th>Height</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Primary</strong></td><td>flag red / white</td><td>The single affirmative action in view: Approve, Send, Mark sent, Email via Maya</td><td>tertiary-container (#9b1c1f)</td><td>44 / 30</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Secondary</strong></td><td>navy / white</td><td>High-emphasis secondary when a primary already exists: Run audit, Download pack</td><td>primary-container</td><td>44 / 30</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Ghost</strong></td><td>surface, navy ink, 1px border</td><td>Neutral and inline actions: Filter, Reset, Clear, Show all</td><td>surface-alt fill</td><td>44 / 30</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Destructive</strong></td><td>error-surface / error-text</td><td>Reject, delete, un-approve</td><td>darker error surface</td><td>44 / 30</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Board primary</strong></td><td>teal #0f766e / white (WIP, cash)</td><td>The one board-local primary; counts as the viewport's primary</td><td>#115e59</td><td>32</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="ds-dodont">
      <div class="ds-do"><h4>Do</h4><ul><li>Label with the verb and the object: "Mark sent", "Approve claim".</li><li>State the non-effects in the confirm: "This does not email anything."</li><li>Grey a button that has no data and keep its tooltip alive.</li><li>Put a link that downloads (<code>a.cfx-btn</code>) in the same row as buttons; they share the class.</li></ul></div>
      <div class="ds-dont"><h4>Don't</h4><ul><li>Two flag-red buttons in one view.</li><li>Gold or green buttons of any kind.</li><li><code>pointer-events: none</code> on a disabled control — the tooltip dies with it.</li><li>Find a button by position in a card; use <code>[data-kpi-btn]</code> hooks.</li></ul></div>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="pills" title="Status pills & badges">
    <p>A pill is a word with a fill. Every status, yes/no, tier and TBD is a pill; a pill without a word is a bug. Geometry: 2px 9px padding, 999px radius, 11px, 600–700 weight, no wrap.</p>
    <DsSpec label="Shell health badges" code=".health-badge .health-ready | -watch | -blocked">
      <span class="health-badge health-ready">Ready</span><span class="health-badge health-watch">Watch</span><span class="health-badge health-blocked">Blocked</span>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Runtime pill with signal dot" code='.runtime-pill[data-tone="ready|watch|blocked"] > .signal-dot'>
      <span class="runtime-pill" data-tone="ready"><span class="signal-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>WorkOS session</span>
      <span class="runtime-pill" data-tone="watch"><span class="signal-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Local auth</span>
      <span class="runtime-pill" data-tone="blocked"><span class="signal-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Supabase pending</span>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Board pills (canonical five tones + brand)" code=".pill .pill-green | -yellow | -orange | -red | -grey | -brand">
      {[["green", "#137a4d", "#e3f5ec", "Paid"], ["yellow", "#946400", "#fbf0d4", "Renewal due"], ["orange", "#a4480d", "#fbe7d6", "Moderate"], ["red", "#a51f1f", "#fbe2e2", "Overdue"], ["grey", "#5a6573", "#eceff4", "TBD"], ["brand", "#11133f", "#e7e8f5", "PA 1042"]].map(([n, fg, bg, label]) => (
        <span style={`display:inline-block;padding:2px 9px;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;line-height:1.5;background:${bg};color:${fg}`} title={`.pill-${n}`}>{label}</span>
      ))}
      <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;padding:2px 9px;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;background:#e3f5ec;color:#137a4d" title=".pill-pay"><input type="checkbox" style="width:13px;height:13px;margin:0;accent-color:#137a4d" checked /> Pay</span>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Popup chips (Territory Map InfoWindow)" code=".vmpop-chip .chip-ok | -muted | -pa | -expired">
      <span class="vmpop-chip chip-ok">Covered</span><span class="vmpop-chip chip-muted">Out of drive time</span><span class="vmpop-chip chip-pa">PA 1042</span><span class="vmpop-chip chip-expired">Expired Jun 30</span>
    </DsSpec>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Tone</th><th>Means</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>green</strong></td><td>Good, yes, healthy, paid, live, in-force</td><td>Paid · Ready · Approved · Live</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>yellow</strong></td><td>Needs attention, partial, late, provisional</td><td>Renewal due · Watch · In review · Sent</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>orange</strong></td><td>Moderate severity (variance 3–6%)</td><td>Moderate</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>red</strong></td><td>Problem, no, overdue, blocked, major</td><td>Overdue · Blocked · Rejected · No agreement</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>grey</strong></td><td>Neutral, out of scope, TBD, unknown</td><td>TBD · Closed · Inactive · Unknown</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>brand</strong> (navy / info)</td><td>Identity or reference, not status</td><td>PA 1042 · Draft · vendor branch</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li><code>TBD</code> is always grey. It is the honest signal for "not wired yet", never a blank cell.</li>
      <li>Confidence tiers (credit-memo matching) are five labelled tones with tooltips: Exact / Confident = green, Probable / Weak = yellow, No match = red. A weak tier must never read like a confirmed match.</li>
      <li>"Review (UOM)" is a pill, never a fabricated number across mismatched units.</li>
      <li>A lapsed price list reads "Extended (awaiting replacement)", yellow — never an error.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="kpi" title="KPI & metric cards">
    <p>Chris's law (2026-06-17): a KPI box navigates to a better view or conveys a decision-relevant number, or it does not exist. On the boards, every pill is a work queue with a count and a button; numbers that never change what the human does next are context and live in subtext.</p>
    <DsSpec label="Shell metric card" code='.live-metric-card[data-tone] > span + strong + small' layout="block">
      <div class="live-metric-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px">
        <a class="live-metric-card" href="#kpi" data-tone="ready"><span class="eyebrow">Open audits</span><strong>14</strong><small style="color:var(--text-muted)">3 blocked on pricing</small></a>
        <a class="live-metric-card" href="#kpi" data-tone="review"><span class="eyebrow">Expected credit</span><strong>$48,210</strong><small style="color:var(--text-muted)">across 9 invoices</small></a>
        <a class="live-metric-card" href="#kpi" data-tone="critical"><span class="eyebrow">Overdue</span><strong>6</strong><small style="color:var(--text-muted)">past 60 days</small></a>
        <a class="live-metric-card" href="#kpi"><span class="eyebrow">Memos sent</span><strong>6</strong><small style="color:var(--text-muted)">this week</small></a>
      </div>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Board KPI pills (each is a filter button)" code=".cfx-kpi / .fw-kpi — aria-pressed toggles the row filter" layout="block">
      <div class="cfx" style="margin:0;padding:12px;min-height:0;border-radius:8px"><div class="cfx-kpis">
        <button class="cfx-kpi" type="button" aria-pressed="true" style="border-color:var(--navy)"><span class="cfx-kpi-lab">To collect</span><span class="cfx-kpi-val">$66,900</span><span class="cfx-kpi-sub">12 jobs · expected this week</span></button>
        <button class="cfx-kpi" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="cfx-kpi-lab">To invoice</span><span class="cfx-kpi-val">$50,680</span><span class="cfx-kpi-sub">2 jobs</span></button>
        <button class="cfx-kpi cfx-kpi-bad" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="cfx-kpi-lab">Overdue 60d+</span><span class="cfx-kpi-val">$18,420</span><span class="cfx-kpi-sub">1 job</span></button>
        <button class="cfx-kpi cfx-kpi-warn" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="cfx-kpi-lab">Stale close-outs</span><span class="cfx-kpi-val">7</span><span class="cfx-kpi-sub">off the board by default</span></button>
      </div></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Pipeline KPI (a direction, not three backlogs)" code=".iv-kpi-flow — 51 → 32 → 3 with a coloured left edge per question" layout="block">
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px">
        {[["Claim it", "var(--primary)", "51 → 32 → 3", "open · with lines · approved", "Approve 3"], ["Chase it", "var(--warning)", "12", "sent, awaiting vendor", "Mark received"], ["Pay it", "var(--success)", "$142,300", "cleared to pay", "Verify paid"], ["Fix it", "var(--text-muted)", "9", "UOM · no-price · routing", "Open queue"]].map(([lab, edge, val, sub, btn]) => (
          <div style={`display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:3px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid ${edge};border-radius:14px;padding:13px 15px`}>
            <span style="font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:600">{lab}</span>
            <span style="font-size:22px;font-weight:750;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">{val}</span>
            <span style="font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted)">{sub}</span>
            <button class="button button-secondary button-small" style="align-self:flex-start;margin-top:6px" type="button">{btn}</button>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Anatomy: uppercase 10–11px label · 22–30px 800 value with tabular numerals · 10.5–13px subtext · optional one button.</li>
      <li>Tone attributes: <code>data-tone="ready|review|critical"</code> on shell cards; <code>.cfx-kpi-bad</code> / <code>-warn</code> on boards.</li>
      <li>A KPI that filters carries <code>aria-pressed</code> and the toolbar's filter label names it with a "Clear filter ✕".</li>
      <li>Grids: 4-up in the shell (2-up ≤ 1180); boards use <code>auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr)</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="tables" title="Tables">
    <p>The table is the primary chart of this app. Uppercase muted headers, tabular numerals right-aligned, labels left, zebra rows on boards, sticky header, optional frozen first column, and the ten-row pane. Status lives in pills inside cells.</p>
    <DsSpec label="Board table in a ten-row pane with show-more" code=".cfx-tablewrap > .cfx-table.cfx-frozen · .cfx-showmore" layout="block">
      <div class="cfx" style="margin:0;padding:12px;min-height:0;border-radius:8px">
        <details class="cfx-group" open>
          <summary class="cfx-group-head" style="cursor:pointer;list-style:none"><span class="cfx-group-name">▾ Denver</span><span class="cfx-group-count">63 jobs · showing 5</span><span class="cfx-group-money">$113,250.00 outstanding</span></summary>
          <div class="cfx-tablewrap cfx-pane" style="max-height:220px">
            <table class="cfx-table cfx-frozen">
              <thead><tr><th>Job #</th><th>Client</th><th>Office</th><th>Rep</th><th class="num">Contract</th><th class="num">Balance due</th><th>Expected</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                {jobs.map((j) => (
                  <tr><td>{j[0]}</td><td>{j[1]}</td><td>{j[2]}</td><td>{j[3]}</td><td class="num">{j[4]}</td><td class={`num ${j[5] === "$0.00" ? "" : ""}`}>{j[5]}</td><td>{j[6]}</td><td><span style={`display:inline-block;padding:2px 9px;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;background:${j[7] === "Collect" ? "#fbf0d4" : j[7] === "Closed" ? "#eceff4" : "#e3f5ec"};color:${j[7] === "Collect" ? "#946400" : j[7] === "Closed" ? "#5a6573" : "#137a4d"}`}>{j[7]}</span></td></tr>
                ))}
                <tr class="cfx-endrow"><td>Total</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class="num">$113,250.00</td><td class="num">$67,380.00</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <button class="cfx-showmore" type="button">Show all 63 jobs  ▾  (58 more)</button>
        </details>
      </div>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Shell queue table (reading density)" code=".queue-table-wrap > .queue-table" layout="block">
      <div class="queue-table-wrap"><table class="queue-table" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse"><thead><tr><th style="padding:13px 14px;text-align:left">Invoice</th><th style="padding:13px 14px;text-align:left">Vendor</th><th style="padding:13px 14px;text-align:left">Office</th><th style="padding:13px 14px;text-align:left">Status</th><th style="padding:13px 14px;text-align:right">Expected credit</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>INV-4821</td><td>ABC Supply · Denver #412</td><td>Denver</td><td><span class="health-badge health-ready">Ready</span></td><td style="text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">$5,140.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>INV-4822</td><td>SRS · Richardson TX</td><td>Dallas</td><td><span class="health-badge health-blocked">Blocked</span></td><td style="text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">$2,980.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>INV-4823</td><td>QXO · Aurora</td><td>Denver</td><td><span class="health-badge health-watch">In review</span></td><td style="text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">$7,420.00</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Board</th><th>Shell</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Header</td><td>10–11px caps, 0.03em, muted, sticky (<code>position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 3</code>), opaque panel background</td><td>12px caps 800, muted</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cell</td><td>12.5px, 4px 8px, <code>white-space: nowrap</code>, 1px bottom border</td><td>14px, 13px 14px, 1px bottom border</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Row height</td><td>29px</td><td>~46px</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Zebra</td><td>even rows <code>--zebra</code>, painted on <code>td</code> (sticky cells need it)</td><td>none</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hover</td><td><code>--fill-bg</code> amber tint on <code>td</code></td><td>none</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Numbers</td><td><code>.num</code>: right, tabular; negative <code>.cfx-neg</code> red</td><td>right, tabular</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Frozen column</td><td><code>.cfx-frozen</code>: first column sticky left, min 200px, 6px shadow; header corner z 4</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>End row</td><td><code>.cfx-endrow</code>: 2px navy top rule (gold in dark), bold</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Section row</td><td><code>.cfx-secrow</code>: zebra fill, 10.5px caps</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Breach cell</td><td><code>.cfx-breach</code>: white on red</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Wrapper</td><td><code>overflow: auto</code> on both axes; max-height measured for 10 rows</td><td><code>overflow-x: auto</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Layout</td><td><code>border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 0</code> (sticky needs it)</td><td>collapse</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h3>Sort, group, filter, page</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Default sort is money-first:</strong> offices and branches by at-risk descending; invoices by date then at-risk; lines by absolute variance descending. Categories by <code>sort_order</code> from the DB, never alphabetically.</li>
      <li><strong>Group before you widen:</strong> lines group into collapsible roof-system category sections (default-collapsed); a 15-column detail becomes a labelled <code>dl.detail-grid</code>, never a 15-wide table.</li>
      <li><strong>Filters apply before paging;</strong> the ten shown are the first ten matching rows; a parent hides when all its children hide.</li>
      <li><strong>Column-group expand state is global</strong> across offices so the eye can track a column down the page; recompute <code>colspan</code> on expand.</li>
      <li><strong>Empty state names the way out</strong> ("Nothing left to audit … Switch to Due now or All").</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="toolbar" title="Toolbar & filters">
    <p>The board toolbar is one row: <em>search · scope select(s) · scope control · More filters · spacer · runtime pill · count · theme trio</em>. Flex-wrap, gap 10px, margin-bottom 16px. It went from ten controls to four on Invoice Audit (docs/100) and that is the ceiling.</p>
    <DsSpec label="Board toolbar" code=".cfx-toolbar / .iv-toolbar / .fw-toolbar" layout="block">
      <div class="cfx" style="margin:0;padding:12px;min-height:0;border-radius:8px"><div class="cfx-toolbar">
        <h2 class="cfx-title">Friday AR Meeting board</h2><span class="cfx-sub">Set expected cash dates · 3-week cash map</span><span class="cfx-spacer"></span>
        <label style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px">Office <select class="cfx-input" style="width:auto;text-align:left"><option>All offices</option><option>Denver · GM 34%</option><option>Fort Collins · GM 31%</option></select></label>
        <label style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px">Rep <select class="cfx-input" style="width:auto;text-align:left"><option>All reps</option></select></label>
        <span class="runtime-pill" data-tone="ready"><span class="signal-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Live</span><span class="cfx-count">10:41 AM</span>
        <div class="cfx-theme" role="group" aria-label="Theme"><button type="button" class="is-active">System</button><button type="button">Light</button><button type="button">Dark</button></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)"><span>Filtered: Office Denver · KPI To collect</span> <button class="cfx-btn" type="button" style="padding:2px 8px;font-size:11px">Clear filter ✕</button></p></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Search</td><td><code>type="search"</code>, placeholder lists what it matches ("Search invoice, item, branch…"), min-width 240px, matches on keyup, hits auto-open their branches.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Office select</td><td>First option is "All PE offices" (value ""). "All" means no constraint, never a synthetic total. Deep links <code>?office=</code> pre-select it and scroll the node into view.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Scope control</td><td>One segmented control answers "which slice am I looking at": To audit · Due now · All. Never three checkboxes.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>More filters</td><td>A <code>details</code> disclosure holding date range and tolerance — real controls, not the first thing competing for attention. Opens as a floating panel (z 20).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Filter label</td><td>When anything is active a line reads the active filters and offers "Clear filter ✕".</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Count</td><td>States the denominator: "5 of 12", or the generated-at time on live boards.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Runtime pill</td><td>live / degraded / pending, from the loader, never assumed.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Theme trio</td><td>Last, right-aligned (see <a href="#theme-control">Theme control</a>).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Composition</td><td>Filters AND across dimensions in one pass; a row is visible when it satisfies all. Rollup bars track the active scope, not the drill filters.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Persistence</td><td>Reveal and open state per surface in <code>localStorage</code>; filters are URL-addressable where a deep link exists.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="segmented" title="Segmented scope control">
    <DsSpec label="Shell segmented control" code=".segmented-control > .segment.is-active">
      <div class="segmented-control"><button class="segment is-active" type="button">All</button><button class="segment" type="button">Ready</button><button class="segment" type="button">Blocked</button></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Board scope control" code=".iv-scope / .cfx-theme pattern — bordered group, active fills navy (gold in dark)">
      <div class="ds-theme" role="group" aria-label="Invoice scope"><button type="button" class="is-active" title="Open, unpaid invoices that still have lines to audit">To audit</button><button type="button" title="Payment due — invoice date + 60 days or older">Due now</button><button type="button" title="Every invoice, including paid and credit memos">All</button></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Two to four options; every option has a <code>title</code> that defines the slice in one sentence.</li>
      <li>Active: navy fill, white text (light); gold fill, navy text (dark). Hover on inactive: navy-soft fill.</li>
      <li>Segment height 32px, radius 9px on the group (4px on the shell's segments), 1px border between segments.</li>
      <li>It is a <code>role="group"</code> of buttons, not radio inputs, so the click handler can dispatch the tree's filter and hidden legacy inputs stay in sync (deep links keep working).</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="inputs" title="Inputs & selects">
