    <ul>
      <li>Depth by border, not shadow. Resting shadow is forbidden; the two shell cards that still carry <code>--shadow</code> at rest (<code>.metric-panel</code>, <code>.gap-metric-card</code>) are recorded drift to remove.</li>
      <li>A Design.md navy <code>.section-head</code> band (white h3, accent eyebrow) is the public-page treatment; inside the app the panel heading is white with a border.</li>
      <li>Two-column list-detail is the dominant page shape: queue left, selected record right (sticky at <code>top: 20px</code>, static ≤ 1180). <code>.wide-left</code> when the list is the primary object.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="queue" title="Queue item & list-detail">
    <DsSpec label="Queue item" code=".queue-item (.is-selected) — navy left rule → accent + lift on hover/selection" layout="stack">
      <button type="button" style="display:grid;gap:4px;width:100%;text-align:left;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--accent);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);color:var(--text);padding:12px 14px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);font:inherit;cursor:pointer"><span style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:8px"><strong>Invoice INV-4821</strong><span class="health-badge health-ready">Ready</span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted)">ABC Supply · Denver #412 · expected credit $5,140.00</span></button>
      <button type="button" style="display:grid;gap:4px;width:100%;text-align:left;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--primary);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);color:var(--text);padding:12px 14px;font:inherit;cursor:pointer"><span style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:8px"><strong>Invoice INV-4822</strong><span class="health-badge health-blocked">Blocked</span></span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted)">SRS · Richardson TX · awaiting price agreement refresh</span></button>
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>The item is a <code>button</code> (or a link when it navigates), full width, left rule navy at rest, accent + selection-lift shadow when hovered or selected. This is the one place a shadow appears on interaction.</li>
      <li>Top line: identifier bold + status pill right; second line: 13px muted context (vendor · branch · money).</li>
      <li>Selecting one loads the detail panel beside it; the list keeps its scroll position and open sections.</li>
      <li>Closing the panel or the nest deselects (recorded bug to fix, docs/59).</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="notices" title="Banners & notices">
    <DsSpec label="Provisional / attention banner" code=".cfx-banner · .snapshot-alert — gold left rule, never a button" layout="stack">
      <div class="cfx" style="margin:0;padding:0;min-height:0;background:transparent"><div class="cfx-banner">Provisional basis (version 0) — fixed-cost pools are placeholders until the CPA rulings land. Numbers here change the week they do.</div></div>
      <div class="snapshot-alert" style="margin:0">Price list extended (awaiting replacement) — the vendor has not issued a new sheet; the last one stays in effect.</div>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Error notice" code=".gap-alert · .cfx-error — error family, states the way out" layout="stack">
      <div class="gap-alert">Territory data failed to load. The map keeps its last snapshot; retry from the toolbar or check the runtime board.</div>
      <p style="margin:0;color:var(--error);font-size:13px">invoice audit query failed: canceling statement due to statement timeout — read through <code>mv_invoice_audit_line</code>, never the view.</p>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Boundary notice" code=".accounting-boundary-notice — states what this surface does not do" layout="block">
      <div class="ds-callout is-info" style="max-width:none"><b>Read-only mirror</b><p>QuickBooks Online is mirror-only here. Nothing on this board writes to QBO; the CSV is loaded by a person.</p></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Gold left rule = attention or provisional; error family = something failed; info blue = a boundary or a fact about the surface.</li>
      <li>A notice never contains the primary action. It may contain a ghost link.</li>
      <li>Notices are one or two sentences and name the way out or the reason; never "Something went wrong".</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="states" title="Empty, loading & error states">
    <p>Never a blank page. Every list, tree and chart has three named states, and the cache worker refuses to snapshot a page still in its loading state.</p>
    <div class="ds-grid-3">
      <div class="ds-card"><p class="eyebrow">Empty (honest)</p><p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px;padding:14px 4px;margin:0">Nothing left to audit — every open invoice has had its lines audited. Switch to <strong>Due now</strong> or <strong>All</strong> to see them.</p><small style="color:var(--text-muted)">.iv-empty — names the way out; no sample fallback, ever.</small></div>
      <div class="ds-card"><p class="eyebrow">Loading</p><p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px;padding:14px 4px;margin:0">Loading invoice detail…</p><small style="color:var(--text-muted)">Text, not a spinner; the shell's <code>pageLooksComplete()</code> keys on it.</small></div>
      <div class="ds-card"><p class="eyebrow">Unavailable</p><p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:13px;padding:14px 4px;margin:0">Cash flow is unavailable: the WIP/AR master has not refreshed since Sep 12. <button class="button button-ghost button-small" type="button" style="margin-top:8px">Open the runtime board</button></p><small style="color:var(--text-muted)"><code>[data-availability="unavailable"]</code> keeps the shell, aligns content to start, offers one action.</small></div>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li>Empty states name the way out; loading states name what is loading; unavailable states name the cause and one action.</li>
      <li>A field that is missing is named ("office not resolved"), never blank; an unwired number is a grey TBD pill.</li>
      <li>Zero coverage shows "—", not "0%". A number that would be a lie is not shown.</li>
      <li>Planned-but-unlive vendors appear in filters with an empty state that says "planned", not "broken".</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="popup" title="Popups & dialogs">
    <DsSpec label="Map popup (InfoWindow) KPI card" code=".vmpop > .vmpop-eyebrow + .vmpop-title + .vmpop-chips + .vmpop-kpis" layout="block">
      <div class="vmpop" style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:12px;background:var(--surface);color:var(--text)"><p class="vmpop-eyebrow">ABC Supply · Branch #412</p><p class="vmpop-title">Denver, CO</p><div class="vmpop-chips"><span class="vmpop-chip chip-ok">Covered</span><span class="vmpop-chip chip-pa">PA 1042</span><span class="vmpop-chip chip-status">active</span></div><div class="vmpop-kpis"><div class="vmpop-kpi tone-ok"><strong>412</strong><span>Priced lines</span></div><div class="vmpop-kpi tone-warn"><strong>14</strong><span>Gaps</span></div><div class="vmpop-kpi"><strong>$1.2M</strong><span>Trailing 12mo</span></div></div><div style="display:flex;gap:6px"><a class="button button-secondary button-small" href="#popup">Invoice audit</a><a class="button button-ghost button-small" href="#popup">Price list</a></div></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Spec</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Popout (board)</td><td>One shared node reused by every row (<code>#fw-guess</code>), <code>role="dialog" aria-modal="false"</code>, anchored to the row, z 40, closes on Escape and outside click. Never one node per row.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>InfoWindow (map)</td><td>232–280px, eyebrow 11px caps, title 15px, chips, 3-up KPI grid, one navy + one ghost small button. The rail's detail card renders the same HTML — two paths to one card.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Dropdown (More filters)</td><td>Absolute below its summary, z 20, panel fill, 10px radius, float shadow.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Confirm</td><td>Native <code>window.confirm</code> today. Text states the scope, the effect and the non-effects ("This does not email anything. It records that you sent the email, moves them to Chase it, and starts the 14-day follow-up clock."). Names every vendor or recipient involved.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Prompt (copy)</td><td><code>window.prompt</code> with the value pre-selected, stating the agent will not send it and when it expires.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Modal</td><td>Not used. A modal that would be needed is a sign the flow belongs on a page.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Toast</td><td>One fixed bottom-centre node, <code>role="status" aria-live="polite"</code>, 2.2s, navy fill (dark: panel + gold rule). Says what happened and whether it persisted: "recalculated locally — not saved".</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="meters" title="Meters & progress">
    <DsSpec label="Review progress (every nesting level)" code=".cc-progress > .cc-progress-head + .cc-progress-track > .cc-progress-fill" layout="stack">
      <div class="cc-progress" style="max-width:360px"><div class="cc-progress-head" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted)"><span>Denver · 412 lines</span><span>318 audited · 77%</span></div><div class="cc-progress-track" style="--line:var(--border)"><div class="cc-progress-fill" style="width:77%"></div></div></div>
      <div class="cc-progress" style="max-width:360px"><div class="cc-progress-head" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted)"><span>Fort Collins · 88 lines</span><span>88 audited · 100%</span></div><div class="cc-progress-track" style="--line:var(--border)"><div class="cc-progress-fill" style="width:100%;background:var(--success)"></div></div></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Match meter" code=".match-score > .meter — smart blue → navy, never flag red">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;max-width:360px;width:100%"><div style="flex:1;height:8px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--surface-alt);overflow:hidden"><span style="display:block;height:100%;width:86%;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--info),var(--primary))"></span></div><strong style="font-size:20px;font-weight:800">86%</strong></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Track 6–8px, radius full, <code>--line</code> / <code>surface-alt</code> fill; fill transitions width over 350ms ease (the one width animation).</li>
      <li>Fill is blue → navy (blue → green on the review checklist), flipping to solid green at 100%. Never flag red.</li>
      <li>Width 74px inline in a summary row (90px at office/branch level); full width in a head.</li>
      <li>Two leaf modes only: DISPOSITION (rolls up DB state) or REVIEW (localStorage checkbox). Lazy subtrees declare <code>data-cc-total</code> so they roll up before mounting.</li>
      <li>A 100% review may burst confetti (Agreement Builder) — the one celebratory motion, and only on completion.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="lights" title="Runtime lights">
    <DsSpec label="R / Y / G / unknown with words" code=".rb-light + label — docs/109 D5">
      {[["green", "var(--success)", "Nightly WIP refresh · 02:10"], ["yellow", "var(--warning)", "ABC invoice feed · fresh but empty"], ["red", "var(--error)", "Better Stack monitor · paused"], ["unknown", "var(--text-muted)", "pg_cron job 13 · no telemetry yet"]].map(([n, c, l]) => (
        <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:13px"><i style={`display:inline-block;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:999px;background:${c};box-shadow:0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, ${c} 20%, transparent)`} aria-hidden="true"></i>{l}<small style="color:var(--text-muted)">({n})</small></span>
      ))}
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Thresholds derive from cadence (1.5× late = yellow, 2× = red) so a weekly job is not yellow every Tuesday.</li>
      <li>A paused monitor is red (a blind spot, not a resting state). Fresh-but-empty is yellow. A missing token is yellow "not configured", never a false green.</li>
      <li>Third-party health comes from this app's own pings: 200 = green (D16). Better Stack watches only the site from outside.</li>
      <li>The word beside the dot is mandatory; the legend is rendered once from code.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="theme-control" title="Theme control">
    <DsSpec label="The trio" code='.fw-theme / .iv-theme / .cfx-theme > button[data-set-theme="system|light|dark"]'>
      <div class="ds-theme" role="group" aria-label="Theme"><button type="button" class="is-active">System</button><button type="button">Light</button><button type="button">Dark</button></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Always three options, always in that order, always last in the toolbar's right cluster.</li>
      <li>Wired with <code>initThemePref(root, "[data-set-theme]")</code>; the active class is set by the helper, never by hand.</li>
      <li>7px 12px padding, 12px 600, group radius 9px, 1px border, active navy/white (gold/navy in dark).</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="chips" title="Chips & tabs">
    <DsSpec label="Filter chips" code=".pf-chip (.is-active) — toggleable, 12px, full radius">
      <button class="pf-chip is-active" type="button">Needs review</button><button class="pf-chip" type="button">Exact</button><button class="pf-chip" type="button">Probable</button><button class="pf-chip" type="button">API · non-negotiated</button>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Tabs" code=".pf-tabs > .pf-tab (.is-active: navy text, flag-red underline) — the one place tertiary marks selection" layout="block">
      <div class="pf-tabs" style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)"><button class="pf-tab is-active" type="button" style="border:0;border-bottom:2px solid var(--tertiary);background:none;padding:10px 12px;font:inherit;font-weight:700;color:var(--ds-heading)">Open <span class="pf-tab-count" style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400">12</span></button><button class="pf-tab" type="button" style="border:0;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;background:none;padding:10px 12px;font:inherit;color:var(--text-muted)">Resolved <span class="pf-tab-count">48</span></button><button class="pf-tab" type="button" style="border:0;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;background:none;padding:10px 12px;font:inherit;color:var(--text-muted)">Deferred <span class="pf-tab-count">3</span></button></div>
    </DsSpec>
    <DsSpec label="Accounting mode tabs" code=".accounting-mode-tabs > .accounting-mode-tab — one tab today (Invoice audit)">
      <a class="accounting-mode-tab is-active" href="#chips" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:36px;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--primary);color:#fff;font-weight:700;font-size:13px">Invoice audit</a>
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Chips filter; tabs switch views; segments choose a scope. Do not use one for another's job.</li>
      <li>Tabs carry counts as muted numerals; a tab with a count of zero still renders.</li>
      <li>The tab underline is the one place flag red marks selection rather than action — recorded as legacy; new tab strips use navy.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="vendor-marks" title="Vendor marks & map markers">
    <DsSpec label="Legend as rendered on the Territory Map" code=".vendor-map-legend > span > i.legend-ring | .legend-badge | .legend-territory">
      <div class="vendor-map-legend" style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:12px;font-weight:850;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--text-secondary)">
        <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px"><i class="legend-ring" style="display:inline-block;width:13px;height:13px;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;border:3px solid var(--success);box-sizing:border-box"></i> Covered</span>
        <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px"><i class="legend-ring" style="display:inline-block;width:13px;height:13px;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;border:3px solid var(--warning);box-sizing:border-box"></i> Renewal / routing</span>
        <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px"><i class="legend-ring" style="display:inline-block;width:13px;height:13px;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;border:3px solid var(--error);box-sizing:border-box"></i> No agreement</span>
        <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px"><img class="legend-badge" src="/vendor-icons/pe-office-badge.png" alt="" width="18" height="18" /> PE office</span>
        <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px"><i class="legend-territory" style="display:inline-block;width:15px;height:11px;border-radius:3px;background:rgb(15 118 110 / 13%);border:2px solid rgb(15 118 110 / 85%);box-sizing:border-box"></i> Office territory</span>
        <span class="legend-note" style="text-transform:none;font-weight:600;opacity:.75">Ring = coverage lens</span>
      </div>
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Marker = vendor logo on an opaque white disc, ring by the highest-priority active condition (routing problem → pricing problem → brand). Clusters are navy discs scaled 12/15/18.</li>
      <li>PE offices carry the roof badge (46px) so our locations read differently at a glance; office territories are teal translucent polygons.</li>
      <li>The rail detail card and the marker popup are the same HTML; assign-office lives in the popup.</li>
      <li>Vendor colour identifies; ring colour signals; the word in the legend explains. Never recolour a logo.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <div class="ds-rules">
    <DsRule id="CMP-01" title="Reuse the component in this chapter before writing a new class; a new component needs a spec entry here and a specimen first." source="Design.md 'Adding to the system'; DSN-014">
      <p>Search this page and <code>global.css</code>. If it exists under another prefix (<code>.fw-</code>, <code>.iv-</code>, <code>.cfx-</code>), copy the canonical one.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-02" title="Every status is a pill with a word; TBD is grey; a fake number is never shown in place of a pill." source="docs/40 §3; CONVENTIONS §10c">
      <p>"Review (UOM)", "Extended (awaiting replacement)", "TBD".</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-03" title="A KPI navigates or informs, and on a board every pill is a work queue with a count and a button." source="Chris 2026-06-17; kpi-pills.ts (Chris 2026-08-09)">
      <p>Context numbers live in subtext. Vanity counts are removed.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-04" title="Tables: sticky header, tabular right-aligned numbers, zebra on td, ten-row pane with a show-more that states the cost." source="standards/design/v1.md § Long-list; docs/40 §2">
      <p>Filters before paging; parent hides when children hide; measured heights only.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-05" title="The toolbar is at most: search · office · scope control · More filters · spacer · runtime pill · count · theme trio." source="docs/100 toolbar 10 → 4">
      <p>A fifth primary control is a sign the surface is two surfaces.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-06" title="Progressive disclosure is native details/summary with one chevron per level; interactive controls inside a summary stop propagation." source="docs/40 §5; friday-wip.astro:755-758">
      <p>Re-rendering preserves open state; Uncategorized is never hidden.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-07" title="Every list has an empty state that names the way out, a loading state in words, and an unavailable state with the cause and one action." source="invoice-audit-tree.ts:856-870; docs/90 honest empty states">
      <p>No sample fallback, no blank page, no spinner-only loading.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-08" title="Confirmations state scope, effect and non-effects and name every party; disabled controls keep their tooltip." source="docs/100 §mark-sent; docs/88 §33-35">
      <p>Approve activates only when every claim line carries a human acknowledgment.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-09" title="One shared popout / toast node per surface; toast is role=status, 2.2s, and says whether the change persisted." source="friday-wip.astro:107; invoice-audit.astro:194">
      <p>"recalculated locally — not saved" is the model.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-10" title="Drill-down links carry scope (?office=, ?branch=) and the target pre-filters and scrolls on land; an unknown branch scopes the search so the page honestly shows empty." source="docs/40 §6; invoice-audit-tree.ts:936-959">
      <p>Never dump a link to the bare entry page.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-11" title="Buttons are found by data hooks, never position; state is changed by clicking the control, never by setting .checked." source="docs/100 §41-46, §22-24">
      <p>Assigning <code>.checked</code> does not fire <code>change</code>, and the toolbar silently disagrees with the tree.</p>
    </DsRule>
    <DsRule id="CMP-12" title="Resting shadow is forbidden; shadow appears on hover, selection and floating layers only." source="Design.md Elevation; docs/40 §2">
      <p>The two shell metric cards with resting shadow are recorded drift.</p>
    </DsRule>
  </div>

  <script>
    // Board specimens use the cash-surface stylesheet, whose dark palette keys on the
    // surface's own data-theme. Mirror the page theme onto every specimen board so the
    // top-bar trio switches them too.
    const root = document.getElementById("ds-root") as HTMLElement;
    const sync = () => document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".cfx").forEach((el) => (el.dataset.theme = root.dataset.theme));
    sync();
    new MutationObserver(sync).observe(root, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ["data-theme"] });
  </script>
</DesignSystemShell>
